## reading
# * compile, gather, cite, answers lint, search, impact, exact, state: ONE resolve_view each, of the pinned view; no tip re-resolution outside
#   it (the only symbolic git read outside resolve_view is HEAD:<domain>/govbridge -- the bridge code tree id, not a view ref).
# * why and history: ONE resolution each -- but of config/canonical-view.yaml, NOT the pinned view: neither CLI accepts --view and neither
#   honours the task spec's view, so both answered from records 46cf1e6 (the live tip after the orchestrator's 20:41 commit) while every
#   other operation of this audit used 7bd7598. The recorded refs do equal the commits used, but the operation cannot be re-run at a
#   recorded view -> INT-D09.
# * impact, search, exact, state outputs and every supplementary packet manifest record NO resolved view -> INT-D15.
## R1-XC pass-5 residuals, assessed
# (1) compile/bootstrap.py resolves the view 6 times per run: CONFIRMED (bootstrap probe: resolve_view=6); harmless only while the view is
#     pinned (all 6 gave records 7bd7598); with config/canonical-view.yaml (records follow: tip) a commit between the 6 splits one bootstrap
#     across two records commits. Worker-facing (the canonical worker bootstrap). LOW while the bridge branch is frozen during a demonstration.
# (2) lifecycle.show_many N+2: standalone module CLI, not dispatched by govbridge/cli.py -- ACCEPTED as residual.
# (3) authority/layer.classify_hit latent re-resolution (commit=None): no caller passes commit=None (grep) -- ACCEPTED.
# (4) exact.show / cite --commit <live branch>: an explicit branch argument resolves that branch's live tip by design; exact show records
#     'commit' in its output -- ACCEPTED; but see INT-D14 for exact grep --ref <view ref name> (crash) / <branch> (live tip).
